title: ActTwoNotes
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The audience
style: note
---
Act II, one day at the castle, a separate root scene with no child. The Countess wants the survey and the old border. A page of the charter is missing, with three clues (the library, the tomb in the castle's chapel, the steward's desk). The steward offers money for a map with his border. The cook's feast sends the cartographer back to the village and back. The act ends when the page is found, or in the evening, with news of a collapse in the mine. #line:ActTwoNotes_0100
===

title: Events
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The audience
quest: audience
when: once
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: here() == "Castle"
---
The gate of Varne castle stands open. Corvin waits in the yard, with his hands behind his back. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Castle_0100
<<if $road == Road.Corvin>>
    Corvin: Our cartographer! The one with a sensible eye. The Countess is waiting in the great hall. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Castle_0200_Corvin
<<elseif $road == Road.Miller>>
    Corvin: The miller's friend. The Countess is in the great hall. Try not to draw her a mill. #mood:angry #line:Events.3344e1f8_Castle_0300_Corvin
<<else>>
    Corvin: The Countess is in the great hall. She has been waiting since morning. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Castle_0400_Corvin
<<endif>>
<<set $quest_audience to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed audience>>
===

title: Events
act: Castle
location: Anywhere
scenario: The collapse
when: once
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: ($quest_audience == QuestState.Succeeded and $quest_page == QuestState.Succeeded) or time_of_day() == "evening" or time_of_day() == "night"
---
// The end of the second act: news from the mine. The path to the mine is a journey, from the castle or the village.
A boy runs in, black with dust to the eyebrows. #line:Events.2716d0bd_0100
Boy: The old gallery fell in! Foreman Gudrun says Jory is under the hill, and the lamps won't reach him. #line:Events.2716d0bd_0200_Boy
Boy: She says the map maker knows the old ways. Will you come? #line:Events.2716d0bd_0300_Boy
<<if $quest_audience != QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<set $quest_audience to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed audience>>
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_page != QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<set $quest_page to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed page>>
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_feast == QuestState.Active or $quest_feast == QuestState.Offered>>
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed feast>>
<<endif>>
<<set $act to Act.Mine>>
<<set $corvin_at_castle to false>>
<<set $corvin_in_mine to $offer != Offer.Accepted>>
<<set $pell_at_castle to false>>
<<go MineRoad>>
===

title: Ysolde
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The audience
quest: audience
when: here() == "Castle" and $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_audience == QuestState.Active
---
Ysolde: The cartographer. Show me what you have. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0100_Ysolde
<<if $quest_survey == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Ysolde: Five landmarks, every one where it should be. My grandfather would have liked you. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0200_Ysolde
<<else>>
    Ysolde: [plural value={survey_count()} one="One landmark" other="% landmarks" /]. I paid for five. #mood:angry #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0300_Ysolde
<<endif>>
-> Tell her about the stones. <<if $culprit != Culprit.Unknown>> #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0400
    <<if $culprit == Culprit.Lio>>
        Ysolde: The miller's child moves them back? To where? #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0500_Ysolde
        Ysolde: Under the hill. That is what my grandfather said, too, when nobody listened. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0600_Ysolde
    <<else>>
        Ysolde: The sergeant blamed the peddler. How convenient for everyone. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0700_Ysolde
    <<endif>>
-> Tell her about the road. <<if $road != Road.Undecided>> #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0800
    Ysolde: The road is Corvin's concern, and the hearing's. The border is mine. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_0900_Ysolde
-> Say nothing more. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_1000
Ysolde: Here is my concern. My grandfather's charter describes the old border between Varne and the abbey. Four pages. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_1100_Ysolde
Ysolde: The third page is missing. It is the one that says where the border runs. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_1200_Ysolde
Ysolde: Find it, and the hearing is ours. Ottilie, in the library, will help you. #line:Ysolde.40406bb3_1300_Ysolde
<<set $quest_audience to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed audience>>
<<set $quest_page to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed page>>
===

title: Ysolde
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
quest: page
when: here() == "Castle" and $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_page == QuestState.Active
---
<<if $clue_library or $clue_tomb or $clue_desk>>
    Ysolde: You are on its trail. I can see it in your face. #line:Ysolde.2cc997aa_0100_Ysolde
<<else>>
    Ysolde: The library first. Ottilie has kept those shelves for thirty years. #line:Ysolde.2cc997aa_0200_Ysolde
<<endif>>
===

title: Ysolde
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
quest: page
when: here() == "Castle" and $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_page == QuestState.Succeeded
---
Ysolde: In Corvin's desk. My own steward. #line:Ysolde.b7b0d6ac_0100_Ysolde
Ysolde: The border is carved under the hill. The miners call them the lantern folk. Nobody has been down there in forty years. #line:Ysolde.b7b0d6ac_0200_Ysolde
<<if $feast_served>>
    Ysolde: And you fed my table, too. I will not forget it. #line:Ysolde.b7b0d6ac_0300_Ysolde
<<endif>>
===

title: Ysolde
act: All
location: Anywhere
scenario: The audience
when: $act != Act.Castle
---
=> Ysolde: The abbey wants our meadows. My grandfather would have laughed at them. #line:Ysolde.fb1791f7_0100_Ysolde
=> Ysolde: Corvin is useful. Useful people are dangerous. <<if here() == "Castle">> #line:Ysolde.fb1791f7_0200_Ysolde
=> Ysolde: Draw it true, cartographer. That is all I ask today. <<if $act == Act.Fair>> #line:Ysolde.fb1791f7_0300_Ysolde
=> Ysolde: The whole valley is watching that table. <<if $act == Act.Fair>> #line:Ysolde.fb1791f7_0400_Ysolde
===

title: Ottilie
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
quest: page
when: $quest_page == QuestState.Active and not $clue_library
---
Ottilie: The charter? Four pages, in my keeping since I was a girl. Three of them. #line:Ottilie.fb80cf44_0100_Ottilie
Ottilie: The third page went out of this library once. The old chaplain, Brother Aldric, borrowed it the winter he died. #line:Ottilie.fb80cf44_0200_Ottilie
Ottilie: He is buried in the castle's chapel. Perhaps he took it with him. Chaplains are like that. #line:Ottilie.fb80cf44_0300_Ottilie
<<set $clue_library to true>>
<<detour PageClue>>
===

title: Ottilie
act: All
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
when: always
---
=> Ottilie: Mind the dust. It's older than both of us. #line:Ottilie.4882f6fb_0100_Ottilie
=> Ottilie: Maps and charters, cartographer. The two lies a valley tells about itself. #line:Ottilie.4882f6fb_0200_Ottilie
=> Ottilie: You found it! Corvin has been borrowing my keys, then. <<if $quest_page == QuestState.Succeeded>> #line:Ottilie.4882f6fb_0300_Ottilie
===

title: Shelves
act: All
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
---
Rolls of parchment, bound ledgers, a box of seals. On one shelf, an old map of the valley with the mine drawn as a little lantern. #line:Shelves_0100
===

title: Tomb
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
quest: page
when: $quest_page == QuestState.Active and not $clue_tomb
---
Brother Aldric's tomb, in the castle's chapel. On the lid, carved under his name: #line:Tomb.27ef1586_0100
"I gave back what I borrowed, to the steward of my day. The border runs where the light sleeps under the hill." #line:Tomb.27ef1586_0200
The steward of his day. The steward's desk, then. #line:Tomb.27ef1586_0300
<<set $clue_tomb to true>>
<<detour PageClue>>
===

title: Tomb
act: All
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
when: always
---
The chaplain's tomb. Somebody leaves fresh flowers here. #line:Tomb.f137e006_0100
===

title: Desk
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
quest: page
when: $quest_page == QuestState.Active and not $clue_desk
---
<<if $clue_library and $clue_tomb>>
    The steward's desk. In the bottom drawer, under ledgers of the castle's flour, a page of old parchment. #line:Desk.d24a02e5_0100
    The third page of the charter. "From the bridge stone, the border runs north under the hill, as the carvings show, to the abbey's well." #line:Desk.d24a02e5_0200
    Corvin's own seal is on the wax that held it shut. #line:Desk.d24a02e5_0300
    <<set $clue_desk to true>>
    <<detour PageClue>>
<<else>>
    The steward's desk, neat as a new grave. You don't know what to look for yet. #line:Desk.d24a02e5_0400
<<endif>>
===

title: Desk
act: All
location: Castle
scenario: The archive
when: $quest_page != QuestState.Active or $clue_desk
---
Ledgers, quills, and a little bottle from Nan's cottage, labelled "for sleep". #line:Desk.af1f93c1_0100
===

title: PageClue
act: Castle
location: Castle
quest: page
---
// Said after each clue to the missing page.
<<if $clue_library and $clue_tomb and $clue_desk>>
    You have the missing page. #line:PageClue_0100
    <<set $quest_page to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed page>>
<<else>>
    One more clue to the missing page. #line:PageClue_0200
<<endif>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The steward's offer
when: here() == "Castle" and $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_audience != QuestState.Succeeded
---
Corvin: The Countess first, cartographer. Then come and see me in my study. #line:Corvin.2bebe375_0100_Corvin
===

title: Corvin
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The steward's offer
quest: offer
when: here() == "Castle" and $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_audience == QuestState.Succeeded and $offer == Offer.NotMade
---
// The third fork: the steward's money, refused, or refused with his letter kept as proof.
Corvin: Sit. You have seen the Countess, and she has told you about her grandfather's border. Under the hill, and so on. #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0100_Corvin
Corvin: Here is a more useful border. The abbey's meadows on our side of the line. The road straight through the village. #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0200_Corvin
Corvin: Draw it so, and it is worth {$bribe} crowns to you. The terms are in this letter. Read it. #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0300_Corvin
<<set $quest_offer to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed offer>>
-> Take the crowns. Draw his border. #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0400
    <<set $offer to Offer.Accepted>>
    <<give crowns {$bribe}>>
    <<give false_map>>
    Corvin: A sensible cartographer. Here is the line I want. Make it look old. #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0500_Corvin
-> Refuse. #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0600
    <<set $offer to Offer.Refused>>
    Corvin: Then we will see whose map the hearing believes. #mood:angry #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0700_Corvin
-> Refuse, and keep the letter. #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0800
    <<set $offer to Offer.Proof>>
    <<give letter>>
    Corvin: My letter, if you please. #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_0900_Corvin
    Corvin: No? Keep it, then. Paper burns. #mood:angry #line:Corvin.ec7da23a_1000_Corvin
<<set $quest_offer to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed offer>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The steward's offer
when: here() == "Castle" and $act == Act.Castle
when: $offer != Offer.NotMade
---
<<if $offer == Offer.Accepted>>
    Corvin: Old ink, cartographer. Brown, not black. Nobody believes a new map. #line:Corvin.957f8688_0100_Corvin
<<elseif $quest_page == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Corvin: You have been in my desk. That page proves nothing. Paper says what you want it to. #mood:angry #line:Corvin.957f8688_0200_Corvin
<<else>>
    Corvin: Still here? The castle is not short of people who say no to me. #line:Corvin.957f8688_0300_Corvin
<<endif>>
===

title: VillageRoad
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast != QuestState.Active
---
The road goes down to the village. The Countess expects you here today. #line:VillageRoad.d750ccf2_0100
===
